57631	57740	57748	57748	Trenchard	351	" Sir Montacute had placed no limit to his son 's expenditure . He did not quarrel with Rowland 's profusion , for his own revenues were ample ; but he _ did _ object to the large sums lavished by him in the service of a faction he was resolved not to support . Accordingly , the old knight reduced his son 's allowance to a third of its previous amount ; and , upon further provocation , he even went so far as to alter his will in favour of his daughter , Aliva , who was then betrothed to her cousin , Sir Cecil Trafford . "
